    "narrative": "Our top offensive priority for today\u2019s slate is **Tyler Soderstrom**, who paces the squad with a 71.98 efficiency score. His matchup against Kumar Rocker is amplified by a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole, offering high ceiling potential for counting stats. Close behind is **Mickey Moniak** (69.71), whose elite platoon advantage against the right-handed Landen Roupp, coupled with favorable wind conditions, makes him a primary engine for our production. **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start at 69.44, as his inherent profile in our scarcity-driven model\u2014driven by his elite speed and high-leverage order position\u2014keeps him as a top-tier asset even without a confirmed opponent starter.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon dynamics, most notably with **Jose Caballero**. Despite a shaky 5.25 xERA from Shane Bieber, **Jose Caballero** faces a steep 13% penalty due to platoon concerns, yet his 61.85 score keeps him locked in given the high-upside matchup. Conversely, **Brice Turang** faces a significantly tougher assignment against Yoshinobu Yamamoto; while his base projection is solid, the decision to start him is buoyed by wind-out conditions and the critical need to leverage his speed against a difficult pitcher who occasionally surrenders base paths. **Austin Riley** also warrants mention; despite hitting lower in the order, his 61.93 score is heavily bolstered by a 14% skill edge against Brandon Pfaadt and a slow-delivery opponent that improves his SB-related floor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who fell just shy of the active rotation with a 47.95 score. While his placement in the two-hole provides some intrigue, the optimizer prioritized the higher base power potential of our starting core. Managers should keep a close watch on **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Jose Caballero**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Josh Naylor**, as all are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status; any significant shifts in batting order will force a re-evaluation of these scores. Finally, please note that **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined on the IL, while **Trevor Story**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** are excluded from today\u2019s active pursuit as we optimize for maximum efficiency across our cap.",
